    {
      "topic": "oil",
      "status": 200,
      "models": [
        "gpt-5.6-luna"
      ],
      "answer": "\u201cMaking oil\u201d usually means fuel is getting past the piston rings into the crankcase, raising the oil level and often making it smell like gasoline. On a 4-stroke, stop running it if the level is rising or the oil feels thin\u2014change the oil and have the fuel system checked, especially the injectors.\n\nOur guide explains the causes and fixes: [Why Mercury FourStrokes Make Oil](https://www.mercuryrepower.ca/blog/mercury-fourstroke-making-oil-guide)",
      "done": true
    },
    {
      "topic": "nmea",
      "status": 200,
      "models": [
        "gpt-5.6-luna"
      ],
      "answer": "Yeah \u2014 here\u2019s our guide: [Mercury Engine Data on Your Garmin, Lowrance or Humminbird: Which Gateway and How to Wire It](https://www.mercuryrepower.ca/blog/mercury-nmea-2000-lowrance-garmin-guide)\n\nIt covers SmartCraft Connect, VesselView Link, the Mercury NMEA 2000 Gateway, compatibility, and wiring basics.",
      "done": true
    },
    {
      "topic": "transom",
      "status": 200,
      "models": [
        "gpt-5.6-luna"
      ],
      "answer": "Before repowering, check the aluminum transom in four ways:\n\n- **Look:** Check around motor-mount holes, seams, corners, and the bottom edge for cracks, corrosion, stains, or bent metal.\n- **Tap:** A solid area sounds crisp; a dull thud can point to a weak or wet core.\n- **Flex:** With the boat safely on the trailer, carefully apply pressure near the motor mounting area and watch for movement.\n- **Seals and fasteners:** Look for loose or enlarged holes, failed sealant, and moisture around bolts and penetrations.\n\nThese are warning checks\u2014not a certification. If anything looks questionable, have a technician inspect it before hanging a new motor.\n\nHere\u2019s our full guide: [The 4-Point Aluminum Transom Check Before You Repower](https://www.mercuryrepower.ca/blog/aluminum-boat-transom-inspection-guide)",
      "done": true
    }
  ],
